Z||000003||PBJ||05-18-2001||09:24 PM||||I would first start with the IAC. (idle air control mtr) it is mounted at throttle plate. Remove and see if you can move it in or out an 1/8 of and inch-if it does not move replace it.<BR>second-check for vacuum leaks, from a vacuum line.<BR>third-with scan tool check coolant temp sensor reading to ecm when cold (at least 4 hours since running) and see if its outside temp, maybe it thinks it is -40 outside and is on high idle.||||reg||1
